{"version":2,"width":80,"height":36,"timestamp":1794645999,"idle_time_limit":2.0,"command":"docs/demo.sh","title":"Serengeti 2.1: a node cut off from its cluster keeps taking writes"}
[0.008873, "o", "\u001b[1mSerengeti: three nodes, one cut off from the other two\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.326772, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m1. Start three nodes on a private network, and a client container\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.654361, "o", "       n1, n2 and n3 are up, and each reaches both peers\r\n"]
[6.656398, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m2. Create a table and insert a row through n1 (a normal, majority write)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.827806, "o", "   n1  INSERT bolt qty=120  -> 200\r\n"]
[8.829833, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m3. Read it on every node\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.16547, "o", "   n1  bolt=120\r\n"]
[9.244104, "o", "   n2  bolt=120\r\n"]
[9.324215, "o", "   n3  bolt=120\r\n"]
[11.326322, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m4. Cut n3 off from n1 and n2 (iptables drops its packets to them)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[15.018317, "o", "   n3  reaches 0 of 2 peers (/v1/status)\r\n   n1  reaches 1 of 2 peers\r\n"]
[17.02092, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m5. A normal write on n3 needs a majority, so n3 refuses it\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[17.070794, "o", "   n3  INSERT washer qty=50  -> 503\r\n"]
[17.106042, "o", "       1 of 3 nodes are reachable; writes need 2 (or send \"ack\": \"local\" to \r\n"]
[17.10852, "o", "       accept it on this node and merge later)\r\n"]
[19.11076, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m6. Write with \"ack\": \"local\" on both sides, changing bolt on each (n1 last)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[19.159233, "o", "   n3  INSERT washer qty=50  -> 200\r\n"]
[19.209163, "o", "   n3  UPDATE bolt qty=100   -> 200\r\n"]
[20.257324, "o", "   n1  INSERT nut qty=300    -> 200\r\n"]
[20.3062, "o", "   n1  UPDATE bolt qty=90    -> 200\r\n"]
[22.30821, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m7. Each side sees only its own writes\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[22.47142, "o", "   n3  bolt=100 washer=50\r\n"]
[22.631232, "o", "   n1  bolt=90 nut=300\r\n"]
[22.712097, "o", "   n2  bolt=90 nut=300\r\n"]
[24.714086, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m8. Heal the network, and wait until every node returns the same rows\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[27.187406, "o", "   n3  reaches 2 of 2 peers\r\n"]
[27.430848, "o", "       all three agree within 4 s of healing; bolt=90, the later write, won\r\n"]
[27.514317, "o", "   n1  bolt=90 nut=300 washer=50\r\n"]
[27.596626, "o", "   n2  bolt=90 nut=300 washer=50\r\n"]
[27.681124, "o", "   n3  bolt=90 nut=300 washer=50\r\n"]
[29.683155, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m9. SHOW CONFLICTS keeps both writes to bolt, the current one first\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[29.853841, "o", "   n2  bolt=90 current from n1; bolt=100 from n3\r\n"]
[31.855818, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m10. One more write to bolt has seen both versions, so it resolves the conflict\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[31.911842, "o", "   n2  UPDATE bolt qty=95    -> 200\r\n"]
[32.309451, "o", "   n1  conflicts: none; bolt=95 nut=300 washer=50\r\n"]
[32.467055, "o", "   n2  conflicts: none; bolt=95 nut=300 washer=50\r\n"]
[32.625685, "o", "   n3  conflicts: none; bolt=95 nut=300 washer=50\r\n\r\n"]
[32.625711, "o", "All expectations held (32 s).\r\n"]
[33.052385, "x", "0"]
